# The standards a composition works under. One row per `asrt:citation` on a composition: the
# instrument as a taxonomy and a value, the clause where one is named, and the edition read.
#
# A consolidation is performed under a rule
#   This is where the composer names it. The regime says which framework the members reported
#   under; the citation says which instrument governs the act of combining them. Two different
#   questions, and only one of them was storable at all without this table.
#
# Read by no rule
#   Homeless for the same reason `eliminations/between.sqlc` was: repeating, read by no rule,
#   therefore under no pressure to exist. Two are filed in this corpus.
-- asrt:composition/asrt:citation, one row each.
SELECT c.composition, c.seq, c.taxonomy, c.instrument, c.clause, c.version
FROM pm.composition_citation c
